[[Jelly|Jellies]] can be assigned as a [[Slayer task]] at level 52 [[Slayer]] and level 57 [[Combat level|combat]] by various medium-level [[Slayer masters]]. They are found in the [[Fremennik Slayer Dungeon]]. They are popular to kill similarly to [[hellhound]]s due to their high drop rate of [[clue scroll (hard)|hard clue scrolls]]. While fairly weak, jellies have an unusually high Defence level compared to other similar monsters around their level.

It is not recommended to kill normal jellies in most circumstances as they have a fairly poor drop table and are very far from a bank.

Two stronger variants of jellies can be found on Zeah; the [[Warped Jelly]] in the [[Catacombs of Kourend]], and the [[Chilled jelly]] in the [[Ruins of Tapoyauik]]/[[Grimstone Dungeon]].

Warped jellies are in a [[Multicombat area]] and are popular for barrage tasks, along with having a better drop table and the Catacombs table. Chilled jellies are in a single combat area and require completion of [[The Heart of Darkness]] or level 87 [[Sailing]]; they have the exact same table as warped jellies (except without the Catacombs table and including [[frozen tear]] and [[Tooth half of key (moon key)|moon tooth half]] drops if fought in the [[Ruins of Tapoyauik]]), but have a 50% susceptibility to fire spells. Despite their higher Magic level, they are still easy to hit with magic.

Players who are assigned jellies by [[Krystilia]] can kill them in the [[Wilderness Slayer Cave]], where nine jellies can be found in a multicombat area. As this location is in the Wilderness, players should be mindful of the risk they bring and not bring items they are unwilling to lose, as the cave is a popular player killing hotspot. There is only one entrance to the jellies and they are below level 30 [[Wilderness]], so players can easily escape with a one-click teleport such as a [[royal seed pod]] if any player killers arrive.

